{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_slice_7", "label": "Slice 7 \u2014 Delete That Is Not Deletion", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A Phase-4 roadmap item pulled forward on the owner's priority call, shipping the subset a Phase-1 user can hit today: a library you can remove things from. Storage tiering stays in Phase 4, because tiering is what makes quarantine's physical layout matter."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_soft_delete_route", "label": "DELETE /api/parts/{id} \u2014 Soft Delete", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "One UPDATE, because every read path already filters part.deleted_at IS NULL, so hiding the part needs no query changes."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_restore_route", "label": "POST /api/parts/{id}/restore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Undelete stays explicit, for the reason delete does: we do not un-delete implicitly either."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_rescan_does_not_resurrect", "label": "A Re-Scan Does Not Resurrect a Deleted Part", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "library_holds must keep not filtering deleted_at \u2014 the load-bearing exception. Deleting from the index is a decision; a scan re-adding it would make delete useless. Both branches already produce it: unchanged bytes hit the hash short-circuit, changed bytes hit the source_path constraint and classify_write. Zero code, and untested until this slice."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_purge_recomputes", "label": "Purge Recomputes ref_count, Never Decrements", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A counter maintained only by arithmetic drifts, and the thing that acts on the drift deletes bytes. Recomputing from reachability makes drift self-heal on the one path that matters. The doomed hashes are collected before the delete, because afterwards there is no path from the part to its blobs; and it is not a race, because UPDATE blob SET ref_count = (subquery) takes the same row lock ingest's +1 takes."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_quarantine_timestamp", "label": "Quarantine Is a Timestamp, Not a quarantine/ Tree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Deviates from DATA.md 1.6. Restore is then free \u2014 clearing the column restores the blob \u2014 where a physical move needs the reverse move and needs every reader to know a second location, a second lookup on the hot path to serve a case that is supposed to be rare. And the store's layout is about to move anyway."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_reaper_sweep", "label": "The 30-Day Reaper Sweep", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Re-asks reachability inside the transaction that deletes the row and the file. On day one it removes nothing, because no row is 30 days old; the destructive path is proved with an injected cutoff, never a wall clock. Re-ingest un-quarantines by existing."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_schema_is_the_safety_property", "label": "The Schema Is the Safety Property, Not the WHERE Clause", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Corrected by the mutation proof: dropping the NOT EXISTS pair for ref_count = 0 does not lose bytes, because file.blake3 and derivative.blake3 are foreign keys to blob and the DELETE raises a constraint violation instead. What the pair buys is availability \u2014 the sweep is one transaction, so one wrongly-quarantined blob would otherwise roll back every legitimate removal beside it, every hour, forever, with a log line as the only symptom."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_eviction_wording_boundary", "label": "The Eviction Wording Boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Three actions, three vocabularies. Eviction is not a deletion with softer words: it removes only bytes we produced and can reproduce, which is why it is the one of the three that needs no undo. The strings are cheaper to get right before there are two of them."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_removed_bytes", "label": "LibraryStorage.removed_bytes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Both storage totals exclude soft-deleted parts, so a removal dropped the number while the disk held the same bytes \u2014 a panel reporting a removal as a saving, the one claim this area must never make. Quarantined bytes are not in it and cannot be: a purged blob has no part and therefore no library, library-less by construction rather than unimplemented."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_refcount_non_load_bearing", "label": "ref_count Is Non-Load-Bearing for Destructive Decisions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The response to a corpus audit that covered only the simple path was not a bigger corpus but removing the counter from every destructive decision, so the audit's coverage stops gating the slice. A drifted counter can waste disk or trigger a quarantine the reaper declines to complete; it cannot destroy a reachable blob. The counter becomes a fast hint and a number to show the user."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_revisionless_part_hole", "label": "A Part With Zero Revisions Is in Neither List", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "page's revision LATERAL is an inner join, so such a part would be beyond reach once removed. Closing it means a LEFT JOIN and a null case on every downstream field of the grid's hottest query, for a state nothing in Phase 1 produces. Phase 2, which is the first thing that can create one, owns it."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_slice_7", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_slice_6b", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_soft_delete_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_part_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_restore_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_soft_delete_route", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_rescan_does_not_resurrect", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_holds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_rescan_does_not_resurrect", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_migration_0007", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_rescan_does_not_resurrect", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_purge_recomputes", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_purge_recomputes", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_quarantine_timestamp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_purge_recomputes", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_refcount_non_load_bearing", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_reaper_sweep", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_7_storage_lifecycle_design_quarantine_timestamp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-7-storage-lifecycle-design.md", "source_